1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:07,008
The five block areas sum to twenty-three, and moving them does not change that total.

2
00:00:08,098 --> 00:00:15,570
The fixed outline has area eighty, so outline density remains twenty-three divided by eighty.

3
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:23,004
Now look at the bounding box, the smallest rectangle that encloses all the placed blocks.

4
00:00:24,094 --> 00:00:30,870
This layout has a nine-by-three box, with just four units inside it left unoccupied.

5
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:37,752
If another layout makes the bounding box smaller, does outline density also increase?

6
00:00:39,492 --> 00:00:46,748
Watch the blocks repack into a six-by-four box, area twenty-four, leaving one empty unit inside.

7
00:00:47,838 --> 00:00:54,446
Outline density stays fixed while packing density increases; the two ratios answer different questions.

8
00:00:55,536 --> 00:01:03,392
Real chips also need connections and routing space, so this lesson compares only its stated area objective.
